  "question": {
    "text": "Suppose for a differentiable function $h, h(0)=0, h(1)=1$ and $h^{\\prime}(0)=h^{\\prime}(1)=2$. If $\\mathrm{g}(x)=h\\left(\\mathrm{e}^x\\right) \\mathrm{e}^{h(x)}$, then $g^{\\prime}(0)$ is equal to:",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "UJDHV",
      "text": "5",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "mVkns",
      "text": "4",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
